# ============================================================
#  THE HOLLOW STAR, v2, Act IV: convergence (docs/plots/hollowstar-v2.md).
#  New cards; hs_last_winter (the opener) and hs_isolde_summons keep their ids where they were.
#    hs_dumont_letter  the Dumonts' mother is coming south for the Blossom moon
#    hs_go_down_early  go down before the deadline: the cult's circle is half-formed, and only those who promised come
# ============================================================

@event hs_dumont_letter
title: A Letter From the North
thread: hs_convergence
actor: kael
when: met(kael) and rel(kael) >= 5
class: story
tone: tense
weight: 16
art: letter
tags: mystery hollowstar
scene: A pale young man holding a letter sealed with a black star at arm's length, as if it might bite, frost creeping up the paper from his fingers.
text: Kael finds you in the library and puts a letter on the table between you without a word. Black-star seal, broken. One line, in a beautiful hand: "I will be at the lake for the Blossom moon. Be there, my son, and bring your friend." It's signed "Mother".{seen(kael_letter_home) > 0: It's her answer to the one he rewrote eleven times.|} His hands are shaking. "She has never come south," he says. "She has never once called me that."
> left: Burn it together
  hint: He'll remember who held the match.
  rel kael +medium
  alignment +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: You hold it over a candle between you until the black star curls. The flame burns blue, then white, then out, and leaves frost on the candlestick. "She'll know," Kael says. "Good." It's the most like his sister you've ever heard him sound.
> right: Keep it. Know your enemy.
  hint: Useful. He won't like it.
  lore +small
  rel kael -tiny
  say: You fold it into your notes. Kael watches you do it and says nothing, which is worse than if he had. That night you read the line again by lamplight. The handwriting is beautiful, and patient, and very sure of itself.

@event hs_go_down_early
title: Before They're Ready
thread: hs_convergence
place: lakeshore
slot: night
class: story
tone: tense
when: final_year and month <= 8 and flag(star_key) and (clue(seven_locks) or clue(ilse_truth)) and hs_called()
repeat: 2
weight: 30
art: door
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
# The early descent (v2, decision 2026-10-26): go down before the Blossom moon. The Night starts at once: the cult's
# circle is half-formed (easier odds against it), but only the allies who promised (winter_*) come with you.
scene: A frozen lakeshore at night, a student holding a black star-shaped key up against the moon, a boathouse door ajar behind them.
text: The lake is freezing in circles tonight, and the key in your pocket is so cold it burns. The Dumonts' mother is coming for the Blossom moon. Her circle isn't ready yet, and neither is the headmistress's. If you went down tonight you'd catch them all unready, and you'd have only the ones who promised you beside you.
> left: Go down tonight
  hint: The Night, now. Only the allies who promised come.
  flag hs_early
  advance hollowstar to 12
  queue hs_the_night now
  say: You walk down to the boathouse without telling anyone. As you lift the latch, the whole lake behind you goes white in one breath, from shore to shore, and somewhere under it a bell begins to toll.
> right: Wait for the Blossom moon
  hint: Everyone who'd stand with you will be there. So will everyone against you.
  mood -tiny
  say: You stand on the shore until your feet are numb, then go back up to bed. The ice creaks after you all the way. Not yet.
